			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3921985">
									

<p>I also enjoyed the phrase, though I think it was repeated one too many times and started to lose its effect.</p>
<p>Ultimately, this is like a nice diet mix of Taboo's nomenclative hazard and Bush v Gore's Garber-speak. I think there is a conceptual inconsistency here; that SCP-4022 <em>can</em> be understood implies a minimal degree of syntactical and logical structure, which seemingly could be &quot;recognized&quot; and consumed by&#8230;tGBNitMoHH.</p>
<p>But this is well written, well paced, and I feel that the angst you portrayed in trying to make as much sense with as little communicative structure as possible is a real horror to imagine, so +1.</p>

